WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.234
-Looking good as always, buddy.

00:00:02.234 --> 00:00:03.367
Thank you so much
for coming back to the show.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.534
You know we love you here.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.968
-Thanks for having me.
Thank you very much.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.501
It's amazing to be here.
Thank you.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.601
We always have fun.
We always have fun.

00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:12.834
-If we don't have fun,
we're doing it wrong.

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:14.300
Exactly, buddy.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.300
Yeah, but I have so many things
I want to talk to you about.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:17.367
First of all, congrats.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:19.267
You got nominated
for two Latin Grammys.

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:20.868
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:22.934 --> 00:00:25.901
-With the great Marc Anthony.
-Yes, sir. Yes, sir.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:27.300
-Marc Anthony.
-Yeah, man.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.267
-How do you guys end up meeting
and knowing each other?

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.834
-That was a funny story.

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:37.200
Well, I've been a huge fan
of his music for a long time,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.534
since I was a kid, man.

00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:41.467
So, like, my parents,
they actually raised me, like,

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:43.901
listening to Marc Anthony's
songs, right?

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:47.334
So then, one day, I knew
that he wanted to meet me,

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:50.033
and he was living in Miami,
and I was there in Florida, too.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:53.100
So I received a text,
and that was Marc.

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:56.968
He was saying like, "Yo, bro,
come to hang out to my house."

00:00:56.968 --> 00:00:59.734
I was like, "What?
-You're like, "Is this real?"

00:00:59.734 --> 00:01:02.133
-Marc.
-Yeah.

00:01:02.133 --> 00:01:05.300
-Marc Anthony. Okay, bro.
Let's go. Come on, let's do it.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.200
And then I came to his house,
and we spent -- Wow!

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.234
We spent like at least
eight hours talking, man,

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:16.033
like till 4:00 or 5:00 a.m.,
listening to his new songs,

00:01:16.033 --> 00:01:19.767
listening to my new songs, like,
back in those days.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.701
And it was amazing, man.
Like, we had these --

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.167
-You spent eight hours together?
-Yeah.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:24.367
-You just hit it off.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.734
-Bro, like, we didn't stop
talking about life

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:29.067
and how our Latin culture,

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:31.167
you know, is impacting
all around the world.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.567
So it's beautiful, man.

00:01:32.567 --> 00:01:35.033
You know, like,
having these kind of friends

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:36.167
is always a good idea.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:37.634
-Yeah, yeah, it's a good idea.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:40.467
It's good to have -- Especially
a friend like Marc Anthony.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:42.067
-Yeah, bro. I love him.

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:45.534
He's like a big brother for me.
He's like a big brother for me.

00:01:45.534 --> 00:01:48.300
I love you, Marc.
-He's a legend. He's a legend.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.100
-Yeah, man.
-But then he had you --

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.300
You're one of the groomsmen
of his wedding recently.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.133
-It was the first time
that I was having, like,

00:01:55.133 --> 00:01:56.934
that role in a wedding.

00:01:56.934 --> 00:02:00.934
-Is that Vin Diesel?
-Yeah.

00:02:00.934 --> 00:02:03.868
Yo, that's so funny. Look at me.
I'm like, "Yo, I'm here."

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:06.167
-You're like,
"I'm here, too, guys."

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.767
-I'm like, "I'm in the back."
Don't leave me."

00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:10.133
-You're like,
"Vin, stand in the back.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.434
-I know I'm the youngest.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:15.167
-Oh, is that David Beckham?
Is this a real photo?

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.567
-I think it's Photoshopped,
though.

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.300
-It's Photoshopped.
Yeah, okay, good.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:19.334
-I'm kidding.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.934
-Wait, that's a party
right there.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:23.100
-Yo, man,
that was a nice party.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.133 --> 00:02:26.200
For sure. We had a blast, man.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.067
Like, we had so much fun --
-You did?

00:02:28.067 --> 00:02:29.367
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:29.367 --> 00:02:30.934
-And is this true that it was
also your birthday, too?

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.467
-Yeah.
-While it was his wedding.

00:02:32.467 --> 00:02:34.601
-Yeah, that was so weird,
because he called me.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.968
He was like, "Yo, man,
I'm going to have my wedding.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.300
I want you to be part of it."

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.901
I was like, "Of course.
But when is it?

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:42.234
Because I'm touring, you know,
and we're always busy.

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:43.601
You're busy, too.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.400
So you have to tell me the date
so I can, you know --"

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:46.634
-Work around it.
-Yeah.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:49.400
And then he was like,
"January 28th."

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.133
"Bro, that's my birthday."

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:53.968
-Any other day, man.
Any other day.

00:02:53.968 --> 00:02:56.267
-Like, "Why are you getting
married on my birthday?

00:02:56.267 --> 00:02:58.267
Like, can you change it?"

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.334
"No, man. Sorry."

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.667
-Did you go to the wedding
and pretend

00:03:01.667 --> 00:03:03.133
like it was a party for you?

00:03:03.133 --> 00:03:05.300
-But it was nice, man,
because I didn't spend

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.968
that money,
you know, on my party, so...

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:11.634
-Yeah.
-He paid the cost.

00:03:11.634 --> 00:03:15.033
-Another champagne bottle.
For Marc. For Marc.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.334
Let's have
another champagne for Marc.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:18.267
-He paid my birthday party,
actually.

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.133
-Yeah.
Can we talk about "Don Juan"?

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.234
-Yes, sir.
-"Don Juan."

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:22.567
Look at this right there.

00:03:22.567 --> 00:03:25.467
Now, this -- Did you --
Oh, I know you have tattoos,

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:27.300
but I never saw your back.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:28.534
Is this --
Did you have this tattoo

00:03:28.534 --> 00:03:29.734
before the album or the album --

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:31.133
-You never saw my back?

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:35.000
-No. Usually,
when we hang out at the pool --

00:03:35.000 --> 00:03:36.467
-I would be worried, man.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:38.133
-When we hang out at the pool,
I jump in the pool before you,

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.634
so I never see your back.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:43.000
I would --
By the way, this is a real fact.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:46.767
I will never take my shirt off
next to you in the rest --

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.067
the history of my life.

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.801
I don't want to be
near you shirtless.

00:03:49.801 --> 00:03:51.634
-No, no, but,
like, we were backstage

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:52.701
and we were saying that --

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:53.901
-I wear Spanx in the pool.

00:03:53.901 --> 00:03:56.601
-No, but he's looking, like,
skinny, strong.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:59.834
Right, guys? Like, he's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:03.300
This guy is getting better
every day, like, you know?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:06.567
-Oh -- But what happens?
This is the album.

00:04:06.567 --> 00:04:08.300
You go --
-That's your back.

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.167
-Yeah, I got your back.
I got your back, buddy.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:13.567
-Thank you, man.
-Yeah, no problem.

00:04:13.567 --> 00:04:15.067
-Yeah, that's my new album, man.

00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:18.901
-Did the album title come first
or did the tattoo come first?

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:20.067
-Hmm.

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:21.234
-I ask the tough,
hard-hitting questions here.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:23.501
-No, no, no, no, no, no.
The tattoo came first.

00:04:23.501 --> 00:04:26.000
Yeah, because I --
Like, I work in the whole idea

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:28.133
and the concept of the album,
you know,

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.634
and then I got the tattoo,

00:04:29.634 --> 00:04:33.567
because as soon I knew
that I wanted to be like

00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.534
this character, Don Juan,
for this season

00:04:35.534 --> 00:04:36.834
just to call it like that,

00:04:36.834 --> 00:04:38.801
then I knew that I had
to get the tattoo.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:41.734
So, yeah, I work around it
and then I had the tattoo,

00:04:41.734 --> 00:04:44.934
and a month later,
I did the cover of the album.

00:04:44.934 --> 00:04:46.634
It was kind of painful, though.

00:04:46.634 --> 00:04:49.434
Because where did you
get the tattoo?

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:50.734
-That was in Miami.
-Yeah.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:52.000
-That was in Miami.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:53.834
-That's a beautiful tattoo.
-It's big.

00:04:53.834 --> 00:04:55.667
Thank God now,
there's these kind of creams

00:04:55.667 --> 00:04:56.968
that they numb you.

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:58.834
Like, they have this numb thing
for the skin,

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:00.234
and you don't feel the pain.

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:02.934
-That's a lot of tattoo.
-That's a lot of ink.

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:04.734
-Yeah, it's a lot of ink.
I don't know -- Yeah.

00:05:04.734 --> 00:05:06.200
-You don't have any tattoos?

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.033
-I don't have any --
I don't know if I could do it.

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:09.467
I can't commit.

00:05:09.467 --> 00:05:13.133
What would I get tattooed --
If I got a tattoo on my back,

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:15.367
what should I put?

00:05:15.367 --> 00:05:16.467
-Well...

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.334
Okay. Don Jimmy.

00:05:18.334 --> 00:05:20.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:23.567
-I'm not putting "Don Jimmy."
My back?

00:05:23.567 --> 00:05:24.834
-Right?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.834
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:31.567
Don Jimmy.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:34.133
-Don Jimmy and Don Juan,
and then we do a duo.

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.267
-We can do a tour together.
-We'll do a duet album.

00:05:36.267 --> 00:05:37.434
Yeah, we'll do a duet.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:39.234
-You know, we switch,
I come do your job.

00:05:39.234 --> 00:05:41.734
Then you go to...
-Yeah, that's a deal.

00:05:41.734 --> 00:05:43.267
I'll do that with you.
-You go to the Garden.

00:05:43.267 --> 00:05:44.367
You perform at the Garden.

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:45.667
-By the way,
Madison Square Garden

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:47.501
