00:06:38.033 --> 00:06:39.767
so it's nice to have them,
you know?

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:42.100
-Yeah. They were there
supporting you from the start.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.868
-Since -- Yeah,
since I started my career.

00:06:43.868 --> 00:06:46.467
I was a little crazy kid
when I started, so --

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:48.367
Thanks, parents. Thank you.

00:06:48.367 --> 00:06:49.868
-Yeah, thank you, mom and dad.
Yeah.

00:06:49.868 --> 00:06:51.133
-Yeah.
-Did I read this right?

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:54.234
Didn't you start almost
as a duo with someone?

00:06:54.234 --> 00:06:56.067
-Yeah. Don Jimmy and Don Juan.

00:06:56.067 --> 00:06:58.367
-Yes, exactly. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:58.367 --> 00:07:01.200
I just want a little credit
for your career.

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:03.834
-Yeah, when I started,
I started with another guy.

00:07:03.834 --> 00:07:05.934
He's from Colombia, too,
from Medellín.

00:07:05.934 --> 00:07:09.200
Hello, Arias.
-Shout-out to Medellín.

00:07:09.200 --> 00:07:13.734
-Yeah. Yeah. Thank you.
Yes, sir.

00:07:13.734 --> 00:07:18.868
So, this guy came late,
super-late to the studio

00:07:18.868 --> 00:07:21.200
the first session that we had.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:24.000
So I decided to make
my first song by my own.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.133
And then we came to the studio.
We recorded the second song.

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:28.601
But to be honest,

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:32.367
I loved the first one more
than the second one with him.

00:07:32.367 --> 00:07:34.601
But -- I don't know -- maybe the
hook was better, you know?

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:35.868
I don't know.

00:07:35.868 --> 00:07:38.567
I just love the way
that the song was sounding.

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:41.367
Sorry, bro, I love it,
but without him.

00:07:41.367 --> 00:07:44.067
-Yeah. But, no, he went on to
have a great career.

00:07:44.067 --> 00:07:45.534
-And now he's a big producer.

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:47.667
He works with Steve Aoki
and he has his own career.

00:07:47.667 --> 00:07:50.434
So, Arias...
-Yeah, he's great.

00:07:50.434 --> 00:07:51.701
-They've been killin' it, man.

00:07:51.701 --> 00:07:52.734
-Everything happens
for a reason.

00:07:52.734 --> 00:07:54.167
-Yeah. Yeah. He's killin' it.

00:07:54.167 --> 00:07:57.033
-I got to say, you're one of the
hardest-working people I know

00:07:57.033 --> 00:07:59.434
and you always do it
the right way

00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:01.234
